mitted as `a41f3f26` with trailer `WI: WI-880`, in `docs/reviews/wi-880/005-ADJUDICATE-9c8a3d7.md`.\n\n**What I saw:** it depends on how the Windows command processor looks up a bare `python`.\n- **In my session:** the reviewer's `[run]` line `cd /d C:\\Python38 && python ...` ran 3.11, which looked like a refutation. But this session sets `NoDefaultCurrentDirectoryInExePath=1`, which turns off the command processor's current-directory lookup.\n- **With that variable unset**, as on an ordinary Windows console, the same line ran **3.8.10** from `C:\\Python38`.\n- **A second route needs no `cd`.** A `python.exe` in the folder the menu starts from ran 3.8 for a plain `python` line, and removing it brought back 3.11. The launchers start every line at the repository root, so a committed `python.exe` there would win.\n\n**Scope:** it's within PROCESS.md §6's review threat model. Both inputs are repository content (a `[run]` line, or a file at the root) running on the stock Windows command processor and real, unmodified interpreters. Nothing requires a compromised host.\n\n**Why FIX:** SR-046 and LLR-047 promise that bare `python` runs on the floor-resolved interpreter \"on every supported platform\". On Windows that's false whenever a line's working folder holds a `python.exe`. I missed it when blessing SR-046 in sitting 003.\n\n**Why not the reviewer's remedy:** I agree with the coordinator that setting `NoDefaultCurrentDirectoryInExePath` for each line's process would change how every bare command in every adopter's Windows lines resolves. A line like `cd tools && mytool` would break. That's a shipped migration far larger than the defect. The coordinator's other argument, that a line which `cd`s into an interpreter's folder has chosen that interpreter, doesn't cover the repository-root route.\n\n**What the lane needs to do:**\n1. Amend SR-046 and LLR-047 to state the Windows exception: a `python.exe` in the line's working folder runs ahead of the menu interpreter.\n2. Add one clause each to the RESYNC_PACK sentence and the `_interpreter_dir` docstring.\n3. If TC-047 gets a test for this boundary, the test must unset the variable explicitly, or this harness hides the route.\n4. Send the amended rows to a fresh amendment sitting.\n\nI changed no code, findings file or registry.","ttft_ms":1518,"type":"result","duration_ms":116300,"uuid":"5c39f32a-0224-45f9-94cc-d3d229fbaa38","ttft_stream_ms":949,"time_to_request_ms":217,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":12,"system_prompt":30,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":1,"input_attachments":127,"input_hooks":1,"transcript_persist":1,"tool_pool_refresh":1,"init_message":8,"engine_pickup":1,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":13,"message_normalization":9,"client_creation":2,"request_build":8},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":47,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":250,"time_to_request_major_faults":7866,"input_attachments_detail":{"slowest_producer":"nested_memory","slowest_producer_ms":81,"cpu_ms":141,"major_faults":3546,"changed_files_reread":4},"first_content_frame_ms":949,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}]
